{
  "title": "Wayward",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Six loops, each",
        "keeping its own",
        "time.",
        "",
        "Record six fragments",
        "from the input and",
        "give each one a",
        "tempo - 100, 101,",
        "102 and so on.",
        "",
        "They start together,",
        "drift apart, and",
        "come back minutes",
        "later.",
        "",
        "Nothing is stretched",
        "to fit. A loop",
        "shorter than its",
        "beat is padded with",
        "silence; a longer",
        "one is cut off at",
        "the wrap.",
        "",
        "The rests are what",
        "make the drift",
        "audible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Getting started",
      "lines": [
        "Drop it into an",
        "audio FX slot.",
        "",
        "1. Press REC 1,",
        " play something,",
        " press REC 1 again.",
        "2. Repeat into 2-6.",
        "3. Press PLAY.",
        "4. Leave it alone.",
        "",
        "Then find SPRD on",
        "the Shape page and",
        "turn it up. That is",
        "the whole module.",
        "",
        "Orbits shows you",
        "what is happening."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Main",
          "lines": [
            "Recording and the",
            "transport.",
            "",
            "REC 1-6 record into",
            "that loop. Press to",
            "start, press to",
            "stop and it begins",
            "looping, press",
            "again to overdub.",
            "",
            "The button names",
            "what the NEXT press",
            "does: REC, STOP,",
            "DUB, PLAY. It only",
            "says so in the",
            "header while held.",
            "",
            "PLAY starts all six",
            "on the same",
            "instant.",
            "",
            "RSYN realigns them",
            "without stopping."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Shape",
          "lines": [
            "How the ensemble is",
            "tuned. Set once and",
            "left.",
            "",
            "BASE is the",
            "reference tempo.",
            "",
            "SPRD fans the six",
            "out from it: loop n",
            "runs at BASE plus n",
            "times SPRD.",
            "",
            "At 0 all six lock",
            "together and never",
            "move. At 1 they are",
            "100 to 105 and take",
            "minutes to separate",
            "and return.",
            "",
            "WIDEN spreads them",
            "across the stereo",
            "field. In mono six",
            "loops turn to mud.",
            "",
            "CLEAR erases every",
            "take over a 15",
            "second fade. Press",
            "again to call it",
            "off."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Loop",
          "lines": [
            "One page for all",
            "six. LOOP picks",
            "which one you are",
            "editing.",
            "",
            "TRIG plays the",
            "window once, now.",
            "",
            "START is where the",
            "window begins.",
            "",
            "END is a LENGTH",
            "from START, not a",
            "second point.",
            "Right of centre",
            "grows it forward.",
            "Left grows it back",
            "and plays it in",
            "reverse.",
            "",
            "BPM and BEAT give",
            "the loop its",
            "length.",
            "",
            "PHAS nudges this",
            "loop by hand. It",
            "slides rather than",
            "jumps."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "FIT modes",
          "lines": [
            "What happens when",
            "the window does not",
            "equal its beat.",
            "",
            "PAD plays it, then",
            "goes quiet until",
            "the loop restarts.",
            "",
            "SPD stretches it to",
            "fill the beat. No",
            "gap, and the pitch",
            "moves.",
            "",
            "RPT repeats it to",
            "fill the beat.",
            "",
            "PADF, SPDF and RPTF",
            "are the same three",
            "with the ends",
            "faded, so the seam",
            "cannot click.",
            "",
            "The plain three",
            "keep the click on",
            "purpose."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Mix",
          "lines": [
            "Every level in the",
            "module.",
            "",
            "1-6 are the loop",
            "faders. They reach",
            "200%, so a quiet",
            "take can be pushed",
            "as well as pulled",
            "back.",
            "",
            "DRY is the live",
            "input. It is not a",
            "crossfade: at full",
            "you hear yourself",
            "and the loops.",
            "",
            "OUT is the level of",
            "the six together."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Orbits",
          "lines": [
            "Where everything",
            "is.",
            "",
            "1-6 show how far",
            "through its cycle",
            "each loop has got:",
            "",
            "-    nothing yet",
            "REC  recording",
            "S    stopped",
            "42   playing, 42%",
            "O42  overdubbing",
            "",
            "Six numbers",
            "climbing at six",
            "rates is the whole",
            "instrument at a",
            "glance.",
            "",
            "ALIGN counts down",
            "to the next time",
            "they all agree.",
            "Past ten minutes it",
            "counts in minutes,",
            "so 12M is twelve."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The drift",
      "lines": [
        "A loop at 100 BPM,",
        "four beats long, is",
        "2.400 seconds. The",
        "same loop at 101 is",
        "2.376.",
        "",
        "Twenty-four ms",
        "shorter: a flam the",
        "first time round.",
        "Fifty times round",
        "they are opposed.",
        "",
        "At a hundred times",
        "round the 101 loop",
        "has run one whole",
        "extra lap, and they",
        "are together again.",
        "",
        "So the relationship",
        "between the numbers",
        "matters more than",
        "the numbers. Tempi",
        "snap to whole ones",
        "for that reason.",
        "",
        "Six loops all at",
        "BEAT 4 realign",
        "every four minutes,",
        "at any whole tempi",
        "at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Notes",
      "lines": [
        "Silence in front of",
        "a take is trimmed",
        "off when you stop",
        "recording, so START",
        "does not have to be",
        "dialled in.",
        "",
        "Settings are never",
        "saved. Wayward",
        "starts at defaults",
        "in every set.",
        "",
        "Takes can run to 30",
        "seconds. That is a",
        "safety net, not a",
        "target.",
        "",
        "Needs Schwung 1.0.0",
        "or newer."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
